      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(status): LINE /status intermittent no-response — fallback, timeout, and retry hardening",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes LINE `/status` intermittently returning no response by hardening the dynamic module loaders, adding a safety-net timeout with fallback message, and cleaning up stale status runtime build checks.\n\n### Changes (10 files, +212/-184)\n\n#### Core Status Fixes\n\n| Phase | What | Rationale |\n|:------|:-----|:---------|\n| **Phase 0+1** | `.catch(() => undefined)` fallbacks on all 4 dynamic runtime loaders | Previously, a transient import failure would propagate uncaught — now each loader returns sensible defaults instead of throwing |\n| **Phase 2** | Eliminate 2 fragile dynamic-import wrappers (`status-message.runtime.ts`, `status-queue.runtime.ts`) via precise static imports; fix `??=` cached-rejection on remaining 3 loaders by resetting promise to `null` on reject | Static imports eliminate the dynamic-hop failure point; promise reset removes the permanent-cache poison so transient failures are retried |\n| **Phase 2 fix** | Replace `?? {} as any` false-positive in plugin health line with proper early-return guard | Previously a loader failure would show \"🔌Plugins: OK\" instead of \"🔌 Plugins: health unavailable\" |\n| **Phase 3** | Add 10s `setTimeout` race in `buildStatusReply` returning a user-visible fallback message | Without the timeout, a hanging render produces zero response to the user |\n| **ClawSweeper fixes** | Revert `warn` → `logVerbose` in `logLineHttpError` (P1); remove proof scripts (P1, behavior covered by unit tests) | `warn` is a theme formatter, not a logger — LINE HTTP errors were invisible |\n\n#### Cleanup\n\n| File | Change |\n|:-----|:-------|\n| `scripts/test-built-status-message-runtime.mjs` + `test/scripts/...test.ts` | Delete stale runtime build checks (superseded by proper unit tests) |\n| `package.json` | Remove `test-built-status-message-runtime` script entry |\n\n#### Tests\n\n| Suite | Tests | Coverage |\n|:------|:------|:---------|\n| `commands-status.test.ts` | 19 | Timeout path (new), throw path, and all existing scenarios |\n| `status-text.test.ts` | 7 | `??=` retry pattern (new, fail → retry → succeed), channel features, plugin health |\n\n### Scope\n\nThis PR targets the specific `/status` no-response failure path only. Broader LINE delivery hardening (reply-token management, push-fallback enhancements) is tracked in a separate open issue: openclaw/openclaw#86012.\n\n### Closes\n\nCloses openclaw/openclaw#94626\n\n---\n\n### Types of Changes\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to change)\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation (non-code change that improves documentation)\n- [ ] 🔧 Chore (refactoring, test updates, CI configuration changes)\n\n---\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nLINE `/status` command intermittently returned no response when dynamic imports through the `??=` pattern suffered a transient failure — the rejected promise was cached permanently, causing every subsequent `/status` attempt to hang indefinitely. Additionally, the timeout safety net was missing entirely: if any segment of the status rendering stalled, the user received zero response.\n\n---\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real environment tested:**\n- **OS:** Windows 11 24H2\n- **Runtime:** Node.js v24.14.1\n- **Branch:** `fix/line-94626-status` (rebased onto upstream/main `574604e3da`)\n\n### Unit test proof\n\n- `pnpm test \"src/auto-reply/reply/commands-status.test.ts\"` — 39 tests pass including:\n  - `\"returns fallback error message when buildStatusText times out after 10s\"` (exercises the timeout race at the integration level)\n  - `\"returns fallback error message when buildStatusText throws\"` (exercises the throw fallback)\n- `pnpm test \"src/status/status-text.test.ts\"` — 10 tests pass including:\n  - `\"falls back on import failure and succeeds when module becomes available\"` (exercises the `??=` promise cache reset)\n- `pnpm test:extensions line` — 14 LINE `send.test.ts` assertions pass with updated `logVerboseMock` expectations\n\n### What this proof covers vs. what it does not\n\n| Aspect | Covered | Not covered |\n|:-------|:--------|:------------|\n| Timeout fallback path | ✅ Integration test through `buildStatusReply` with mocked hanging `buildStatusText` | ❌ Not triggered through a real LINE `/status` command with a genuine hanging import (requires a production LINE bot with the failure condition) |\n| `??=` retry pattern | ✅ Unit test proves promise cache is reset on rejection and subsequent retry succeeds | ❌ Not triggered through a real LINE session |\n| Normal `/status` rendering | ✅ LINE screenshots in PR history show working `/status` output | — |\n| CI | ✅ All CI checks pass on this SHA | — |\n\n### Limitations\n\n- The patched timeout/retry fallback was not triggered through a live LINE bot conversation because triggering the genuine failure condition (a transient dynamic import rejection) is environment-dependent and not reproducible on demand. The timeout path is exercised at the integration test level, and the retry path is exercised at the unit test level.\n\n### Maintainer decision required\n\nThis PR adds a **10 second timeout** to every `buildStatusReply` caller. A status render that is slow but would eventually succeed will instead return fallback text after 10 seconds. Maintainers should confirm this behavior is acceptable before merging.\n\n---\n\n## Review status\n\n- ✅ Code review: APPROVED (0 blocking)\n- ✅ Test coverage: PASS (all suites including new timeout and retry tests)\n- ⏳ ClawSweeper review: pending re-review after proof scripts removed\n- ✅ Rebased onto upstream/main (`574604e3da`) — clean rebase\n",
